    "blurb": "The early May 15th Fillmore East show delivers towering versions of Attics Of My Life, The Other One and Dark Star despite a missing right channel in the acoustic set. Jerry’s guitar is on fire and Pigpen’s organ adds sober texture to the quieter numbers. The soundboard capture is clean and balanced, preserving the marathon double‑bill energy.",
    "review": "On May 15, 1970 the Grateful Dead took over Fillmore East for a sprawling early‑show that still feels like an epic journey. After two acoustic sets peppered with Pigpen’s clear organ and occasional vocal spikes, the band launched into electric fireworks – a monster Attics Of My Life, a relentless The Other One segueing into a soaring Dark Star, and a tight Cosmic Charlie finish. Jerry Garcia’s tone was “perfect” on those jams, while Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart drove the rhythms with unrelenting power. Though the acoustic portion suffers from a missing right channel and a brief dropout before Candyman, the overall tape is crisp, low‑hiss, and captures the full double‑bill marathon in impressive detail.",
